{"name":"Backdrop","hex":"#a7a799","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"backdrop","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A decorated cloth hung at the back of a stage.","An image that serves as a visual background."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To serve as a backdrop for."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backdrop"}],"entries":[{"title":"Theater drapes and stage curtains","blocks":[{"text":"Theater drapes and stage curtains are large pieces of cloth that are designed to mask backstage areas of a theater from spectators. They are designed for a variety of specific purposes, moving in different ways and constructed from various fabrics. Many are made from black or other darkly colored, light-absorbing material. Theater drapes represent a portion of any production's soft goods, a category comprising any non-wardrobe, cloth-based element of the stage or scenery. Theater curtains are often pocketed at the bottom to hold weighty chain or to accept pipes to remove their fullness and stretch them tight."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Stage_curtains.jpg/330px-Stage_curtains.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theater_drapes_and_stage_curtains"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6a/Stage_curtains.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6a/Stage_curtains.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Different types of curtains.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStage_curtains.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/PANO_DE_BOCA_DO_THEATRO_MUNICIPAL_DO_RIO_DE_JANEIRO_-_A_INFLU%C3%8ANCIA_DAS_ARTES_SOBRE_A_CIVILIZA%C3%87%C3%83O.jpg/500px-PANO_DE_BOCA_DO_THEATRO_MUNICIPAL_DO_RIO_DE_JANEIRO_-_A_INFL